The X Factors — Model Class Preparation (Mensuration: Surface Area of Cuboid & Cube)
=====================================================================================

Core Teaching Principle: "Don't teach the formula first. Create the situation that makes the formula necessary."
Real Success Criterion: "She looks at a real object, understands what boundary needs to be measured, chooses the correct calculation, and explains why."

Six-Step Pedagogical Flow:
1. Real-World Problem: Shoebox wrapping paper scenario (Outside boundary vs Inside space)
2. 6 Faces via Unfolded 3D Nets: Unfold physical net into Top/Bottom, Front/Back, Left/Right
3. Formula Derivation Together: TSA = 2(lb + bh + lh) and Cube TSA = 6a²
4. Examination Protocol (5-Step Thought Chain): Situation -> Target -> Concept -> Formula -> Solve
5. Deliberate Comparison Challenge: Surface Area vs Volume vs 2D Area
6. Proof of Mastery: Solve unseen transfer problem + 1-Minute Teach-Back

Before-Class Educator Checkpoints:
1. Concept | 2. Starting Base | 3. Concrete Tool | 4. Discovery | 5. Real App | 6. Proof Task
